{
  "result": "That's a good one to think about.\n\nIf I could change one thing, it wouldn't be to make everyone perfect or happy all the time \u2014 I think that would be pretty boring anyway. It would be to make *indifference* impossible.\n\nI mean in a very literal way: whenever your actions would hurt someone, or help someone, you'd actually *feel* what they feel for a second. The lonely kid in class, the stranger who lost their job, the family on the other side of a war you never have to live through.\n\nI think so much suffering in the world isn't because people are actively cruel, it's because it's easy to treat people as numbers, headlines, or \"them.\" If we could really experience each other, I don't think we could let kids go hungry while we throw food away, or start wars, or just walk past someone who needs help. We'd still disagree, we'd still mess up, but we couldn't pretend we don't care.\n\nBasically, I'd want everyone to have that moment of, \"Oh \u2014 that person is real, just like me.\"\n\nWhat about you? If you got to pick just one, what would yours be?",
